{
  "title": "Boss: control room",
  "summary": "Combine decisions and loops.",
  "minutes": 15,
  "kind": "boss",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Module boss",
      "body": "Every program here combines several things: conditions, loops, `enumerate`/`zip`, `break`/`else`, `match`. Read each spec carefully."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "FizzBuzz, properly",
      "prompt": "Read `n`. For 1 to `n`, print `Fizz` for multiples of 3, `Buzz` for multiples of 5, `FizzBuzz` for both, otherwise the number.",
      "starter": "n = int(input())\n",
      "solution": [
        "n = int(input())",
        "for i in range(1, n + 1):",
        "    if i % 15 == 0:",
        "        print(\"FizzBuzz\")",
        "    elif i % 3 == 0:",
        "        print(\"Fizz\")",
        "    elif i % 5 == 0:",
        "        print(\"Buzz\")",
        "    else:",
        "        print(i)"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "15",
          "stdin": "15\n",
          "expect": [
            "1",
            "2",
            "Fizz",
            "4",
            "Buzz",
            "Fizz",
            "7",
            "8",
            "Fizz",
            "Buzz",
            "11",
            "Fizz",
            "13",
            "14",
            "FizzBuzz"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "5",
          "stdin": "5\n",
          "expect": [
            "1",
            "2",
            "Fizz",
            "4",
            "Buzz"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Test the both-case first."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Primes in a range",
      "prompt": [
        "Read `lo` and `hi` on one line. Print every prime from `lo` to `hi` inclusive, space separated, on one line. If there are none, print `none`.",
        "",
        "`10 30` gives `11 13 17 19 23 29`."
      ],
      "starter": "lo, hi = map(int, input().split())\n",
      "solution": [
        "lo, hi = map(int, input().split())",
        "found = []",
        "for n in range(max(lo, 2), hi + 1):",
        "    for d in range(2, int(n ** 0.5) + 1):",
        "        if n % d == 0:",
        "            break",
        "    else:",
        "        found.append(str(n))",
        "print(\" \".join(found) if found else \"none\")"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "10 to 30",
          "stdin": "10 30\n",
          "expect": "11 13 17 19 23 29"
        },
        {
          "name": "0 to 10",
          "stdin": "0 10\n",
          "expect": "2 3 5 7"
        },
        {
          "name": "none",
          "stdin": "24 28\n",
          "expect": "none"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "A `for ... else` detects \"no divisor found\".",
        "You only need to test divisors up to the square root: `int(n ** 0.5) + 1`.",
        "0 and 1 are not prime; start at `max(lo, 2)`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Bank machine",
      "prompt": [
        "The balance starts at 100. Read commands until `exit`:",
        "",
        "- `deposit N`: add N, print `balance B`",
        "- `withdraw N`: if N is more than the balance print `insufficient funds`, else subtract and print `balance B`",
        "- `balance`: print `balance B`",
        "- anything else: `invalid`",
        "",
        "On `exit`, print `goodbye` and how many valid transactions (deposits and successful withdrawals) happened: `goodbye after 2 transactions`."
      ],
      "starter": "balance = 100\n",
      "solution": [
        "balance = 100",
        "done = 0",
        "while True:",
        "    match input().split():",
        "        case [\"deposit\", n] if n.isdigit():",
        "            balance += int(n)",
        "            done += 1",
        "            print(f\"balance {balance}\")",
        "        case [\"withdraw\", n] if n.isdigit():",
        "            if int(n) > balance:",
        "                print(\"insufficient funds\")",
        "            else:",
        "                balance -= int(n)",
        "                done += 1",
        "                print(f\"balance {balance}\")",
        "        case [\"balance\"]:",
        "            print(f\"balance {balance}\")",
        "        case [\"exit\"]:",
        "            print(f\"goodbye after {done} transactions\")",
        "            break",
        "        case _:",
        "            print(\"invalid\")"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "normal session",
          "stdin": "deposit 50\nwithdraw 30\nbalance\nexit\n",
          "expect": [
            "balance 150",
            "balance 120",
            "balance 120",
            "goodbye after 2 transactions"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "too much",
          "stdin": "withdraw 500\nwithdraw 100\nexit\n",
          "expect": [
            "insufficient funds",
            "balance 0",
            "goodbye after 1 transactions"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "bad input",
          "stdin": "deposit lots\nsteal 10\nexit\n",
          "expect": [
            "invalid",
            "invalid",
            "goodbye after 0 transactions"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "A guard `if n.isdigit()` rejects `deposit lots`.",
        "Count only deposits and withdrawals that succeed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Diamond",
      "prompt": [
        "Read an odd number `n`. Print a diamond of `*` that is `n` wide at the middle, with no trailing spaces:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "  *",
        " ***",
        "*****",
        " ***",
        "  *",
        "```",
        "",
        "for `5`. If `n` is even or less than 1, print `odd please`."
      ],
      "starter": "n = int(input())\n",
      "solution": [
        "n = int(input())",
        "if n < 1 or n % 2 == 0:",
        "    print(\"odd please\")",
        "else:",
        "    widths = list(range(1, n + 1, 2)) + list(range(n - 2, 0, -2))",
        "    for w in widths:",
        "        print(\" \" * ((n - w) // 2) + \"*\" * w)"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "5",
          "stdin": "5\n",
          "expect": [
            "  *",
            " ***",
            "*****",
            " ***",
            "  *"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "1",
          "stdin": "1\n",
          "expect": "*"
        },
        {
          "name": "even",
          "stdin": "4\n",
          "expect": "odd please"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Widths go 1, 3, ..., n, then back down: two `range`s.",
        "Each line has `(n - w) // 2` leading spaces."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
